      questions: [
        { n: 11, prompt: "What does the writer say about the prisms above and below the central section of the lens?", options: ["A They allowed the lens to be made from cheaper glass.", "B They redirected light that would otherwise have been wasted.", "C They made the beam visible from all directions.", "D They reduced the weight of the whole apparatus."], answer: "B", explanation: "O texto diz que os prismas 'captured light which would otherwise have escaped and redirected it into the horizontal beam'.", tip: "Nas MCQ, as opções erradas usam ideias verdadeiras noutro contexto (peso, vidro); confirme a relação exata com o elemento da pergunta." },
        { n: 12, prompt: "What point does the writer make about the keepers' logbooks?", options: ["A They show that most keepers were poorly educated.", "B They prove that stations received many visitors.", "C They show that the work included events as well as long periods of dullness.", "D They reveal that the weather was the main danger."], answer: "C", explanation: "Os diários registam 'rescues, visitors and the long monotony of the work', ou seja, acontecimentos e monotonia.", tip: "Uma opção que usa apenas parte do texto (só visitantes, só tempo) costuma ser distrator." },
        { n: 13, prompt: "What is the writer's main purpose in the final paragraph?", options: ["A To argue that lighthouse lenses are still the best technology available", "B To show that Fresnel's idea has continued to be useful beyond lighthouses", "C To criticise the replacement of lenses by LED beacons", "D To explain why museums collect old lenses"], answer: "B", explanation: "O parágrafo termina com exemplos de uso atual: 'Variants of his design appear in car headlamps ... and in the large panels that concentrate sunlight'.", tip: "Para perguntas de propósito, resuma o parágrafo numa frase antes de olhar para as opções." }
      ]
