        { n: 7, prompt: "Delay may result from feeling disconnected from the person one will become.", answer: "B", explanation: "Adeyemi propõe que 'the psychological distance between present and future identity encourages delay'.", tip: "'Disconnected from the person one will become' reformula 'distance between present and future identity'." },
        { n: 8, prompt: "Changing working conditions would help reduce delay more than teaching individuals.", answer: "D", explanation: "Para Ortiz, 'Clearer goals and fewer interruptions would ... reduce procrastination in organisations more effectively than any training course'.", tip: "Cuidado: o autor critica Ortiz, mas a pergunta só pede quem defende a ideia." },
        { n: 9, prompt: "Putting off a task brings a quick emotional reward that encourages repetition.", answer: "A", explanation: "Brevik concluiu que 'Avoiding the task brought immediate relief, and this short-term reward was enough to teach the brain to repeat the behaviour'.", tip: "'Quick reward' = 'short-term reward'; os sinónimos de tempo são pistas fiáveis." }
